			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement output channel lifecycle handlers for Sky\n\nIntroduce a complete suite of Tauri command handlers under `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Output/` to manage the editor's output panel lifecycle. This bridges the Wind service layer with the Sky frontend for displaying and manipulating output streams.\n\nThe implementation adds five new modules adhering to the project's PascalCase naming and `one struct per file` architecture:\n- `OutputCreate`: Acknowledges channel creation and logs to the dev console.\n- `OutputAppend` & `OutputAppendLine`: Emit `sky://output/append` events to stream text into the Sky scroll buffer, with the latter automatically appending newlines.\n- `OutputClear` & `OutputShow`: Emit `sky://output/clear` and `sky://output/show` events respectively, allowing the frontend to reset buffers or bring a specific channel to focus.\n\nThese handlers utilize the `CommonLibrary::IPC::SkyEvent` system to trigger reactive updates in the Sky UI, completing the native backend support for the integrated output terminal.",
			"SHA": "70253806a73d36c1bcc9269c4d4c468497bf3be7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:16:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1339,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement RBAC enforcement engine with audit logging\n\nIntroduce the `PermissionManager` subsystem within `Source/IPC/Security` to enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) on all IPC operations. This module provides the `Manager::Struct` enforcement core, which validates operations against user `SecurityContext` data (roles and permissions) before dispatch.\n\nKey components include:\n- `Manager::Struct`: Maintains role/permission tables and a rolling 1,000-entry audit log. Implements `validate_permission` to gate access and `log_security_event` for telemetry.\n- `SecurityContext::Struct`: The request envelope carrying user identity, roles, and origin IP.\n- `SecurityEvent::Struct` & `SecurityEventType::Enum`: Standardized audit log entries for access grants, denials, and violations.\n- `initialize_defaults`: Bootstraps standard roles (User, Developer, Admin) and permission definitions (file, config, storage, system).\n\nThe implementation adheres to PascalCase naming and the project's modular architecture, ensuring the native backend can strictly enforce least-privilege principles for file I/O, configuration updates, and system extensions.",
			"SHA": "429102af223fb0f5403463c95f8e492f94e7e879"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:16:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1333,
				16
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement IPC message compression and RBAC role engine\n\nIntroduce two critical subsystems within the Mountain backend's `Source/IPC` layer to optimize bandwidth and enforce access control.\n\n**Message Compression & Batching:**\nAdd the `Enhanced::MessageCompressor` module to aggregate IPC payloads before transmission. The `Compressor::Struct` buffers messages until size or time thresholds are met, then flushes using configurable algorithms (Brotli, Gzip, Zlib) and levels. Supporting DTOs (`BatchConfig`, `CompressedBatch`, `CompressionInfo`) provide telemetry and serialization support, reducing network overhead for high-frequency native-to-extension communications.\n\n**Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):**\nEstablish the `Permission::Role::ManageRole` engine with strict `category.action` naming validation. Define the `Role::Struct` and `Permission::Struct` with support for sensitivity flags (e.g., `system.execute`, `role.manage`) to trigger elevated audit logging. Implement factory functions (`CreateAdminRole`, `CreateDeveloperRole`, `CreateUserRole`) to bootstrap the standard security hierarchy, ensuring the IPC layer enforces least-privilege principles across the editor's distributed components.\n\nBoth modules adhere to PascalCase naming and the project's modular 'one struct per file' architecture.",
			"SHA": "a74d4b330ceea060804b0ab8fd5957ac1676f1a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:16:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1315,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement Tauri command handlers for global and workspace storage\n\nIntroduce a comprehensive suite of Wind IPC service handlers under `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Storage/` to bridge the Mountain backend with the editor's persistent storage system. These handlers fulfill the contract required by Wind's `NativeWorkbenchStorageService` to manage state across workspaces.\n\nThe implementation covers the full CRUD lifecycle for both global (cross-workspace) and workspace-scoped storage:\n- **Basic Operations:** `StorageGet` (workspace), `StorageSet` (workspace), `StorageDelete` (global).\n- **Bulk Operations:** `StorageGetItems` (hydrates the UI cache with all global key/value pairs), `StorageKeys` (returns all global keys), and `StorageUpdateItems` (atomic batch insert/delete).\n\nHandlers strictly adhere to PascalCase naming, resolve the `StorageProvider` via `ApplicationRunTime.Environment`, and include atomic locking guarantees for concurrent access. This scaffolding enables the editor to persist extension state, user settings, and workbench configuration reliably on the native filesystem.",
			"SHA": "a03f56da8cabe6362445181dcf079001584a61de"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:16:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1308,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement initial Tauri command handlers for Source Control Management\n\nIntroduce the foundational Tauri command suite under `Source/Command/SourceControlManagement/` to enable the Wind UI to interact with version control systems. This initial batch covers seven core operations: `CheckoutSCMBranch`, `ExecuteSCMCommand`, `GetAllSourceControlManagementState`, `GetSCMBranches`, `GetSCMCommitHistory`, `GetSCMResourceChanges`, and `StageSCMResource`.\n\nThe implementation establishes the Tauri command interface adhering to the project's PascalCase naming convention. While the current logic returns mocked success responses or stubbed data structures (as noted in `TODO` comments), the handlers correctly resolve the `ApplicationState` from the Tauri `State` and access the `SourceControlManagementProviders`, `SourceControlManagementGroups`, and `SourceControlManagementResources` markers.\n\nThis scaffolding bridges the gap between the Sky/Wind frontend and the native backend, paving the way for integrating the `SourceControlManagementProvider` trait implementation to handle real Git operations, uncommitted change prompts, and branch management logic.",
			"SHA": "64057baae447ee1b3540d2f99f9a0fefee8ab2a4"
		}
	],
